Ph.D. programs is highly competitive. Students admitted into either program\u2014at UNC Greensboro or North Carolina A&T State University\u2014are guaranteed two years of departmental assistantship support, with an additional two years available upon achieving Ph.D. candidacy.\nAdditional funding is often available through research assistantships supported by grant-funded faculty, institutional awards from both UNCG and NCA&T, and a range of external fellowships and scholarships. These opportunities are typically merit-based and aligned with student performance. Connecting with a potential research advisor prior to applying can help you identify funding options specific to your interests and goals.\nCurrently, nearly 94% of students receive some form of graduate assistantship and/or tuition waiver.\nNanoengineering\nGraduate Funding\nGraduate Assistantships\nApply for an Assistantship\nExternal Funding Sources\nNanoscience\nGraduate Funding\nGraduate Assistantships\nApply for an Assistantship\nExternal Funding Sources\nApply Today!\nBack to Top\nJoint School of Nanoscience and Nanoengineering\nDean's Office/General Inquiries: 336.285.2810\nFax: 336.271.3333\nGeneral Inquiries: jsnninfo@ncat.uncg.edu\nApply Now\nContact Us\nEmergency Procedures\nLocation: The Joint School of Nanoscience and Nanoengineering\nMailing Address: 2907 East Gate City Blvd. Greensboro, NC 27401\nFollow Us:\nPhysical Address:\n1400 Spring Garden Street\nGreensboro, NC 27412\nMailing Address:\nP.O. Box 26170\nGreensboro, NC 27402-6170\nPhone:\n336.334.5000\nSpartan Safe\nEmployment\nComments\nTitle IX\nUNCG Policies\nSACSCOC/QEP\nBookstore\nTerms of Use\nStrategic Plan\nSitemap\nCampus Accessibility\nReport an Accessibility Issue\nCopyright \u00a92026 UNC Greensboro. All rights reserved.\nBlueSky\nFacebook\nInstagram\nTikTok\nTwitter\nYouTube\nLinkedIn\nSnapchat", "links": [["", "https://www.uncg.edu"], ["Skip to Main Landmark (Press Enter)", "https://jsnn.ncat.uncg.edu/students/funding/#main-